s></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAI HITOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYANARI SETSUKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIYANO SOTARO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MOROHASHI NAOYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>ODO JUNICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEYA HARUHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>AKASHI, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKI, NOBUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAHARA, NOBUKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KUMAGAI, HITOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYANARI, SETSUKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYANO, SOTARO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MOROHASHI, NAOYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ODO, JUNICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEYA, HARUHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Metal complexes which serve as catalysts in various chemical reactions or as materials in the information-electronics industry, exhibit peroxidase-like activities or high hydrolytic activities for phosphoric diesters, and can easily hybridize with base sequence recognition sites; and novel analytical methods for hydrogen peroxide with the complexes exhibiting peroxidase-like activities. The above metal complexes are prepared by bringing a cyclic phenol sulfide represented by general formula (2) into contact with at least one member selected from among Group 8, 1A to 7A, 1B and 3B metals, and are usable as catalysts for the oxidation with hydrogen peroxide or those for the hydrolysis of phosphoric diesters, the hydrolysis catalysts being useful also in the analysis for hydrogen peroxide. In said formula X&lt;1&gt; is hydrogen, a hydrocarbon group or the like; Y&lt;1&gt; is hydrogen, a hydrocarbon group or the like; Z&lt;1&gt; is Sm&lt;1&gt; or the like; m&lt;1&gt; is an integer of 1 to 7; and n&lt;1&gt; is an integer of 4 to 8.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne des complexes métalliques servant de catalyseurs dans diverses réactions chimiques ou de matériaux pour l'industrie de l'information et de l'électronique. Ces complexes présentent une activité peroxydasique ou une grande activité hydrolytique vis-à-vis des diesters phosphoriques. Ils s'hybrident facilement avec les sites de reconnaissance des séquences de base. L'invention concerne également de nouvelles méthodes d'analyse du peroxyde d'hydrogène utilisant les complexes présentant une activité peroxydasique. Les complexes métalliques précités se préparent en mettant le sulfure de phénol cyclique, représenté par la formule générale (2) ci-après, au contact d'au moins un élément choisi parmi les métaux du Groupe 8, 1A à 7A, 1B et 3B. On peut les utiliser comme catalyseurs pour l'oxydation par le peroxyde d'hydrogène ou comme catalyseur pour l'hydrolyse des diesters phosphoriques, ces catalyseurs d'hydrolyse étant utiles également pour l'analyse du peroxyde d'hydrogène. Dans la formule (2), X&lt;1&gt; représente hydrogène, une groupe hydrocarbure ou analogue; Y&lt;1&gt; représente hydrogène, un groupe hydrocarbure ou analogue; Z&lt;1&gt; représente Sm&lt;1&gt; ou analogue; m est un entier compris entre 1 et 7; et n&lt;1&gt; est un entier compris entre 4 et 8.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>